0</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2342;&#2379; &#2330;&#2367;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2346;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>528 &div; 9 - 16 x 4 + 156 = 120</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">4 and 156, + and -</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2324;&#2352; 156, + &#2324;&#2352; -</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">4 and 9, + and -</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4 &#2324;&#2352; 9, + &#2324;&#2352; -</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">528, 156, &div; and x</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">528 &#2324;&#2352; 156, &div; &#2324;&#2352; x</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16 and 9, x and +</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16 &#2324;&#2352; 9, x &#2324;&#2352; +</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Option (a): </p><p>528 &div; 9 - 16 x 4 + 156 = 120</p><p>After interchange:</p><p>528 &div; 9 + 16 x 156 - 4 = 120</p><p>58.6 + 2496  -  4 = 120</p><p>2550.6 is not equal to 120</p><p>Thus this option is not correct. </p><p>Option (b):</p><p>528 &div; 9 - 16 x 4 + 156 = 120</p><p>After interchange:</p><p>528 &div; 4 + 16 x 9 - 156 = 120</p><p>132 + 144  -  156 = 120</p><p>276  -  156 = 120</p><p>120 = 120</p><p>Thus, this option is correct. </p><p>Option (c):</p><p>528 &div; 9 - 16 x 4 + 156 = 120</p><p>After interchange:</p><p>156 x 9 - 16 &div; 4 + 528 = 120</p><p>1404  -  4 + 528 = 120</p><p>1928 is not equal to 120</p><p>Thus, this option is correct.</p><p>Option (d):</p><p>528 &div; 9 - 16 x 4 + 156 = 120</p><p>After interchange:</p><p>528 &div; 16 - 9 + 4 x 156 = 120</p><p>33  -  9 + 624 = 120</p><p>648 is not equal to 120</p><p>Thus, this option is incorrect. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If 'x' means division, '-' means multiplication, '+' means subtraction and '&div;' means addition, then which of the following equation is correct?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 'x' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;, '-' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366;, '+' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; '&div;' &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3 + 69- 11 x 5 &div;9 = 8</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3 + 69- 11 x 5 &div;9 = 8</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">17 &div; 12  -  10 + 15 x 3 = 10</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">17 &div; 12 - 10 + 15 x 3 = 10</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 + 7  -  16 &div; 36 x 18 = 80</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 + 7 - 16 &div; 36 x 18 = 80</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">42 x 6  -  17 &div; 4 + 10 = 113</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">42 x 6 - 17 &div; 4 + 10 = 113</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>3 + 69- 11 x 5 &div;9 = 8</p><p>After interchanging signs, we get:</p><p>3  -  69 x 11 &div; 5 +9 = 8</p><p>So LHS is not equal to RHS</p><p>17 &div; 12  -  10 + 15 x 3 = 10</p><p>After interchanging signs, we get:</p><p>17 + 12 x 10 - 15 &div; 3 = 10</p><p>= 17 + 120  -  5</p><p>= 132</p><p>So LHS is not equal to RHS</p><p>20 + 7  -  16 &div; 36 x 18 = 80</p><p>After interchanging signs, we get:</p><p>20 - 7 x 16 + 36 &div; 18 = 80</p><p>20  -  112 + 2 = 90</p><p>So LHS is not equal to RHS</p><p>42 x 6  -  17 &div; 4 + 10 = 113</p><p>After interchanging signs, we get:</p><p>42 &div; 6 x 17 + 4 - 10 = 113</p><p>=7 x 17 + 4 -10</p><p>=119 + 4- 10</p><p>= 113</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>By Interchanging the given two numbers which of the following equation will be correct?</p><p>3 and 9</p><p>I. 27 &div; 3  X  18 + 9  -  36 = 21</p><p>II. 9  X  12  -  45 &div; 3 + 16 = 109</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2346;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>3 &#2324;&#2352; 9</p><p>I. 27 &div; 3 X 18 + 9 - 36 = 21</p><p>II. 9 X 12 - 45 &div; 3 + 16 = 109</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Neither I nor II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Both I and II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>I) 27 &div; 3  X  18 + 9  -  36 = 21</p><p>After interchanging 3 and 9</p><p>27 &div; 9  X  18 + 3  -  36 = 21</p><p>54 + 3  -  36 = 21</p><p>57  -  36 = 21</p><p>21 = 21</p><p>Thus, equation I is correct.</p><p>II) 9  X  12  -  45 &div; 3 + 16 = 109</p><p>After interchanging 3 and 9</p><p>3  X  12  -  45 &div; 9 + 16 = 109</p><p>36  -  5 + 16 = 109</p><p>36 + 11 = 109</p><p>47 &#8800; 109</p><p>Thus, equation II is incorrect.</p><p>Hence, the answer is an option (a).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>By interchanging the given two numbers (not digits), which of the following equation will be correct?</p><p>10 and 15</p><p>I. 253  -  230 &div; 15 + 10  X  2 = 260</p><p>II. 182 + 10  X  21  -  30 &div; 15 = 15</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; (&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2346;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p>10 &#2324;&#2352; 15</p><p>I. 253 - 230 &div; 15 + 10 X 2 = 260</p><p>II. 182 + 10 X 21 - 30 &div; 15 = 15</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Only I</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Both I and II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">I &#2324;&#2352; II &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Neither I nor II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344; &#2340;&#2379; I &#2324;&#2352; &#2344; &#2361;&#2368; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only II</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>If the numbers 10 and 15 are interchanged, then the equations will be: </p><p>I. 253  -  230 &div; 10 + 15  X  2</p><p>= 253  -  23 + 30</p><p>= 283  -  23 </p><p>= 260. Thus, equation I is correct. </p><p>II. 182 + 15  X  21  -  30 &div; 10</p><p>= 182 + 315  -  3</p><p>= 497  -  3 </p><p>= 494. Thus, equation II is incorrect. </p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}